        "id": 1038039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-10-19T10:31:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "[It\u0027s amazing how often basic arithmetic is messed up (trivial issues like wrong ordering of args when calculating age) or overflow leading to massive negative or positive values. Given this is going to be new code for partners / SoC vendors, and multiple parties are involved, I think it makes sense to be super defensive about negatives, and \"fail\" in a way that should be super obvious. Just converting to zero will just hide a major issue]\n\nIf it\u0027s negative, I think this it should be logged with a warning level or above, and probably the NITZ shouldn\u0027t be passed on at all: one piece of information is corrupt, why should we trust the others? e.g. similar to ignoreNitz.\n\nI also think that ages greater than some threshold should be ignored, but I think we can leave that logic in the NitzStateMachine (once we actually pass the age further downstream, see later review comments about my design doc comments).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 257,
        "startChar": 21,
        "endLine": 257,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "cb2703faa5e57b9f84b98feaa5b0bf9fe1cf9bbf",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
