      "message": "Generally, Java\u0027s case statement scoping default is not great. Since there are several local variables in this \"case\" they will therefore be in scope for other \"case\" / throughout the (very long) method. Blocks are often used to avoid needing to come with alternative var names, or to avoid \"pollution\" between cases.\n\nSo, I suggest adding braces:\n\ncase EVENT_NITZ_TIME: {\n   ...\n   break;\n}\n\nTelephony team\u0027s code, so up to you.",
