      "message": "Can you reset the mNitzStateMachine mock between tests, so that each test block is more self contained...? It seems bad that this test has to \"know\" the previous block made a call and account for it here.\n\nWithout doing that / a comment, then it\u0027s not really clear to the reader why it\u0027s times(2). (It makes it look like you expect 2 calls, which would actually be a bug.)\n\nSuggestion: break out a new test entirely, and call it \"testSetTimeFromNITZStr_withAge()\" (and consider renaming the old one to withoutAge(), since it can be the test that covers the case with the argument missing, not with an explicit zero ageMs).\n\nI\u0027d also be inclined to have a test as part of _withAge() that _explicitly_ passes zero ageMs.",
